# cron alternative to the systemd unit: poll once every five minutes.
#
# Install with `crontab -e`. Do not run this alongside the systemd service or
# alongside loop mode -- they would contend for the same lock. (Contention is
# handled safely, but only one of them would ever do useful work.)
#
# Two cron traps, both of which the script already defends against:
#
#   * cron's PATH is minimal, so `python3` may not resolve. Use an absolute
#     interpreter path.
#   * cron does not give you a useful working directory. All paths inside the
#     scraper resolve relative to main.py rather than the CWD, so this is fine
#     -- but any path *you* pass as an argument must be absolute too.

# Poll every five minutes, appending output to a log.
*/5 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /opt/crypto-price-scraper/main.py --once >> /var/log/crypto-scraper.cron.log 2>&1

# Note: cron starts jobs on a best-effort schedule and can run a few seconds
# late under load, so row timestamps land at roughly :05:03 rather than exactly
# :05:00. The timestamps record when the price was actually observed, which is
# the honest value. Use the systemd unit in this directory if you want exact
# grid alignment.
